@host = http://localhost:5089
@customerToken = paste-the-accessToken-from-a-Customer-login
@adminToken = paste-the-accessToken-from-a-DisputeAdmin-login

### Sign in as a customer
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "thandi@example.test",
  "password": "set-this-in-seed-users.csv"
}

### Sign in as a dispute admin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@capitec.test",
  "password": "set-this-in-seed-users.csv"
}

### The caller's own transactions, each with its dispute state
GET {{host}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 403, because a transaction belongs to a customer and staff have none
GET {{host}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### The caller's own disputes
GET {{host}}/api/disputes
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Every customer's disputes, because the caller is staff
GET {{host}}/api/disputes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Only the disputes that are still initiated
GET {{host}}/api/disputes?status=Initiated
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### One dispute. Paste an id from a list response above
GET {{host}}/api/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The status timeline of that dispute, oldest entry first
GET {{host}}/api/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/history
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Raise a dispute. Paste the id of an undisputed transaction from
### GET /api/transactions. Amount, currency, date and merchant are read off
### that transaction by the server and are not part of the request.
POST {{host}}/api/disputes
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "reason": "Delivered order was missing three items."
}

### 409, raising a second dispute on a transaction that already has one
POST {{host}}/api/disputes
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "reason": "Trying again."
}

### Advance a dispute one step. Two steps at once is a 409
PATCH {{host}}/api/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "UnderInvestigation"
}

### 403, because only a DisputeAdmin can change a status
PATCH {{host}}/api/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "UnderInvestigation"
}
